186045417] [17592186540027 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540027 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(7)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0009\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17398103-0726-57d3-aad8-24938a444c94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540027 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =0.3007.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540036 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540036 #edb/ref 1069 "q-225086" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540036 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540036 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(9)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 8).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0550\\,$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,0.4557\\,$ | $\\,0.5874\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\ge 8)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540036 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27647abc-efb3-57c0-813d-ce357897815d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540036 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 8)=P(X>7).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 8) & =P(X>7) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =1-F(7) \\\\  & =1-0.3239 \\\\  & =0.6761.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540098 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540098 #edb/ref 1069 "q-224966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540098 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540098 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(4<X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ |\n\n$P(4<X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540098 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8455b7b-7c5b-5bab-ac5b-3afa70d37c46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540098 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\})+P(X\\in \\{5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(4<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(4<X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.3134-0.0996 \\\\  & =0.2138.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540124 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186540181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540124 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "15fb34ea-7c36-5de6-89f0-352505c9199d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540124 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186540098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540126 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186540124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540126 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "296bb2e2-9a40-524a-8c06-52de5f6f888d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921